# CRUD UI

List pages show one entity type. Search sits above the list. Create/edit forms do not belong on the list.

- **Add** is a compact secondary header control. Never a primary CTA or inline form on the list page.
- Each list row owns **Edit** and **Delete**. Extra actions (Open, QR) may sit on the same row.
- Create and edit open a **sub-screen**. Delete stays on the list and uses a confirmation dialog.
- Saving meeting or attendee edits: edit fields → Save → confirmation → persist. Do not write on Save alone.
- Every sub-screen has **Back** (or Close). Breadcrumbs are not required.
- Use `confirmAction` from `src/lib/confirm.ts` for delete and save confirmations. Cancel and confirm must both be present.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: create form on the list page
<TextInput placeholder="First name" />
<AppButton title="Add person" onPress={onSave} />
<FlatList data={people} />

// ✅ GOOD: list + row actions; form lives on a sub-screen
<ScreenHeader title="People" actionTitle="Add" onAction={() => router.push(addRoute)} />
<EntitySearch value={query} onChangeText={setQuery} placeholder="Search people" />
```
